package wk:clipboardcompat;

/// The guest side of the wk:clipboard shim: a C or C++ program compiled
/// against wkclip.h reads and writes the HOST's system clipboard, if — and
/// only if — this node is wired to a Clipboard node on the canvas and its
/// capability token still allows the action. The sibling of ../midi-compat's
/// wkmidi world; the interface itself is vendored under wit/deps the same way.
///
/// It is deliberately NOT folded into ../gfx-compat. That world imports only
/// `wasi:` packages — it is the WASI graphics shim, and a `wk:`-custom package
/// in it breaks that invariant. Folding it in would also make doom, quake,
/// mupdf, netsurf, paint, triangle and gfx-smoke each link a clipboard import
/// that none of them uses, which shows up in `wk` as a Clipboard port on every
/// graphical node.
world wkclipboard {
    import wk:clipboard/clipboard;
}
